      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Capsaicin (15 or 100 mg/kg, s.c.) produced thermal analgesia in the rat hot plate test (55 degrees C). Capsaicin (100 mg/kg) also caused a reduction in spinal cord substance P levels. However, the time-course of capsaicin-induced depletion of substance P levels does not correlate with the time-course of thermal analgesia. Also, substance P depletion is biphasic, suggesting that more than one mechanism is involved in capsaicin's ability to reduce substance P levels in the spinal cord."},
